WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.160
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.950
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.950
In our world, the balance between

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.870
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.870
crime and punishment is forever being measured.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.750
When it comes to the sentence
for any given crime,

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.540
someone will say it's fair,
and someone else will say it's too lenient.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.040
This time, it's that kind of story.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.450
"Majima Produce"

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.410
"Majima Produce"

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.410
Uh, excuse me.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.200
"Majima Produce"

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.200
Oh, hello.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.200
You're Makoto Majima-san?

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.660
Yeah, that's--

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.290
Wh-What?

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.620
Please smash this guy's leg.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.830
Huh?!

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.700
Just one leg, left or right.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:53.500
But I want him to be unable to walk
without a cane for the rest of his life.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.330
"Majima Produce"

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.330
Come with me.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.000
"Majima Produce"

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.000
Hey!

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:09.250
"Ikebukuro West Gate Park"

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.870
By the way, what's your name?

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.870
Chihiro Hayama. I work at a West Gate shop.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.000
Are we going somewhere?

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.250
I wanted you to see the scene.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:46.450
"Scene"? What happened?

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:51.830
Exactly a year ago, my brother was working
at an Italian place at the West Gate.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.580
He was on his way home from work, after 11PM.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.160
S-Somebody...!

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.000
Help me...!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.950
His kneecap was busted into pieces.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:23.000
This is where that beast attacked my brother.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.040
All that was stolen was ¥3,000.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.040
So, what happened to the beast?

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.540
He went to jail.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.830
Then isn't that a good thing?

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.790
It isn't good at all!

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:39.290
As a minor, the beast was only
in juvenile detention for seven months.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:42.040
He's already out of jail like normal.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.580
My brother still can't walk without a cane,

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.910
but <i>he's </i>strolling around town
like nothing happened.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:52.120
Thanks to that incident, he can't be
on his feet for long periods of time.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:56.870
So, he can't go on being a cook,
and he quit his restaurant job!

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.200
All over a measly ¥3,000!

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.000
That beast!

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:05.950
All right. Tell me a little more about it.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.120
What's his name?

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.830
Eiji Otokawa.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.540
Why did you come to me?

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.950
I heard it doesn't cost much.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:20.200
Well, good thing you <i>did </i>come to me.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:27.250
Lately, there've been guys all over
the place who'll do any job for money.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:32.160
But hiring somebody like that is very dangerous.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.500
It's common for them to threaten you afterwards

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.700
and demand money beyond what you agreed to pay.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:44.040
For now, tell me everything
you know about Eiji Otokawa.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:48.040
At the end of last year, he got out
of juvenile detention in Nagano Prefecture.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:51.950
He doesn't have any kind of job,
he just lives at home and wanders the town.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.370
Hey, do you really want to smash this guy's leg?

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:58.750
Of course!

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:03.700
If you do that, it'll mean you've
fallen to the level of beast, too.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.540
Think carefully about it.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.250
Still, though.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:17.620
I want that beast to suffer
the way my brother suffers.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:23.910
I want you to wreck his leg.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:32.750
"Big Rei"

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:33.790
"Big Rei"
"Want to go out for drinks sometime?"

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.160
"Big Rei"
"Want to go out for drinks sometime?"

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.160
Oh.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.620
"Chihiro"
"Right now I'm tailing"

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:41.910
"Chihiro"
"the beast"

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.370
Chihiro! Where are you now?!

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:51.750
The arcade at Rosa Kaikan. He comes here a lot.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.870
Don't do anything reckless until I get there!

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.370
Or, at all!

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.500
It's okay, I'm wearing sunglasses.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.750
That's not what I mean!

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:03.870
Hello!

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.620
Hey, Big Rei?

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:07.200
There's something I need to know!

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.790
What, this isn't about what I sent earlier?

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:12.290
Can't go drinking today!

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:14.750
And, sorry, but I'm in a hurry!

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:19.000
His name's Eiji Otokawa.
He got out of juvie recently.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.250
Could you look him up and get back to me?

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.870
All right.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:25.450
That figures.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:28.250
"Rosa Kaikan"

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.450
That's the beast.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:39.160
Looks like one seriously timid beast.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.410
Hello.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:46.080
Okay, hold on a second.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:50.500
And so?

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.870
Eiji Otokawa, age 18. Unemployed.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:59.790
On the street in Ikebukuro,
he struck restaurant worker Tsukasa Hayama

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:02.000
on the shoulder with a cylindrical weapon.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.500
After that, he stomped on the leg
of Hayama, the fallen victim.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:11.330
Hold on a sec. Was the weapon like,
one of those extendable batons?

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:16.370
No, it wasn't. Length, 30cm.
A stainless steel shoehorn.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.620
Shoehorn?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.200
That's right.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:23.000
He was desperate, and that
was something he had at home.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.120
What do you mean desperate?

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.080
Some high school classmates of Otokawa's
were extorting money from him,

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:35.700
and he was told to bring the money--
any amount--by the day after the attack.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:40.080
He testified that, if he hadn't done it,
he'd be the one to get hit.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:48.120
Did the ones extorting money get in trouble?

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:52.410
Yeah. Four of them: Boy A, B, C, and D.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:58.330
But they were all first offenders,
so they just got warnings, not juvie.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.620
In effect, they were acquitted.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:04.250
So, only the bullied kid got sent to juvie?

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.040
Hey, like I always say, this phone call...

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.910
...never happened. Thanks.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:21.620
Otokawa attacked your brother because
he needed money to give to them.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:24.330
He got caught and sent to juvie,

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.830
and the four extorters got off
with a little scolding.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.790
Maybe they want money again.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:38.290
Hey, Chihiro. Would you still
smash Otokawa's leg?

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:39.910
You got that?

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.290
I'm not sure, now.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:48.870
But I'm not just going to do nothing.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:53.330
"Rosa Kaikan"

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.040
"Rosa Kaikan"

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.040
You want to meet my brother?

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:56.120
"Rosa Kaikan"

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:56.120
Yeah. I know how you feel,
but I don't know about his feelings yet.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:09:00.620
"Daily Job Offers"

00:08:56.120 --> 00:09:00.620
Yeah. I know how you feel,
but I don't know about his feelings yet.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:02.620
Besides, if I was your brother,

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:07.160
I don't think it'd sit well with me
if I was kept out of all this.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:11.540
But my brother doesn't know
that guy is back in town.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:13.750
We'll keep that a secret.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:17.370
Why don't we pretend you're
introducing a new boyfriend?

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:18.700
All right.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:25.790
Coming!

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:39.160
Wow. The suit does <i>not </i>work on you.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:43.040
"Episode 10"

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:46.830
Thank you for the invitation.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:48.160
You're welcome.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:53.330
Oh, hey, what about your parents?

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:59.200
They died in a traffic accident
when I was 11.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.700
Oh. Sorry to ask a weird question.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.200
The reason my brother loves to cook

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:09.040
is because he wanted
to have me eat delicious food.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.500
What's all the whispering about?

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:14.250
Here, Makoto-kun. You eat up, too.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:15.870
Thank you.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:32.120
Your brother really is a good cook.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.700
But our dream of starting
a restaurant is gone now.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:38.330
Why? I mean, this is so good.

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:41.000
With a leg braced with titanium wire,

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.040
he can't stand up for longer than three hours.

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.250
It will always be that way.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:48.410
Oh, sorry.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:57.790
Suppose... you met your attacker,
Tsukasa-san. What would you do?

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.660
I don't know.

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:04.250
At first, I thought about stabbing him to death,

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:07.290
and I didn't care if I'd go to prison.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:12.450
But doing that would amount
to committing social suicide.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:17.870
If I met with him directly, looked him
in the eye, and talked with him,

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:20.660
maybe I'd feel a little differently.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:22.830
How come?

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:27.620
Because not all criminals are beasts.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:35.410
If I knew he was human, and not a beast,
maybe my feelings of hatred would change.

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:39.040
I don't want to stand
in a place of hatred forever.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:43.200
I still hate him, but I want to get past that.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:50.830
To not return the hatred,
but to look him in the eye and talk...

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:57.200
I feel like that's when I was taught
what it means to be a noble person.

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:04.950
Oh, welcome home.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.700
What's wrong?

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.080
I saw him.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:17.290
Huh?

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.080
I saw him.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:24.500
Tsukasa...

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:34.290
I saw him.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:37.330
I saw him.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.790
I saw him...

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:45.950
He saw Otokawa?

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:50.410
He's mostly calmed down,
but it was like he wasn't himself.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:54.040
We're out of time. I'll make a move tomorrow.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.450
What will you do?

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:56.620
I have an idea.

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.370
You're Eiji Otokawa?

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:09.120
I'm Makoto Majima.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:14.790
I've been watching you for a while
at a certain somebody's request.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.410
Somebody?

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:17.620
Who?

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:23.870
I also saw your worst friends from
your high school days menacing you.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.700
Would you like to cut ties with those guys?

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:33.700
With just one phone call from me,
you could be a G-Boys member.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:38.660
None of the kids living in this town
would think of threatening a G-Boy.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:40.540
The G-Boys...

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.790
You mean, King's...?

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:48.040
But before I give you this bandana,
I want you to meet with my client.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:51.540
If you won't, you can forget
about the G-Boys deal.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:57.540
I don't really get it, but could
I meet with that person?

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.500
If it'll bail me out...

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.080
I'm right here.

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:10.250
Lately, the Red Angels have been
expanding their influence.

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.580
So I've had more errands to go see to.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:15.580
You didn't have to come here in person.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:20.250
I want to see how you resolve this situation.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.540
This is Otokawa?

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.500
Y-Yes, sir!

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:26.330
Makoto told me about you.

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:30.700
As of this moment, you can consider
yourself a G-Boys member.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:34.370
From now on, if anyone
threatens you, mention my name.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:36.620
Y-Yes, sir!

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:46.790
What's the story behind today?

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:50.830
Suddenly telling me there's
someone you want me to see...

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:52.830
Chihiro is my client.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:56.040
--Huh?
--She wanted me to attack Eiji Otokawa.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:01.620
But rather than produce another casualty,

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:04.540
I decided to gamble on what you told me.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.500
Look him in the eye and say all you want.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.540
"Him"?

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:10.870
Come on over!

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:26.700
Sit directly across from this guy.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.830
He's Tsukasa Hayama-san, the victim you struck,

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:33.290
smashed his knee, and stole his money.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:47.580
Come on, Eiji. Look straight
at the person you attacked.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:50.000
Show him how you truly--

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:58.580
Why did you attack me?
What did you need that money for?

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:02.620
I'm sorry. It could have been anyone.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:05.290
They've always bullied me.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:07.410
If I didn't bring them <i>something</i>,
they would have hit me again--

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:08.870
Cut the crap!

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:10.620
You're going to make it their fault?!

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:13.370
You're saying it's not yours?!

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:17.250
My mother died when I was 12.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:22.790
It was just me and my dad from then on.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:26.080
The bullying started in fifth grade.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:33.620
They told me I stank, that I was
always wearing the same dirty shirt.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:37.200
So what?! We had it even worse!

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:42.450
I got passed from relative to relative
from the time I was 11!

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:44.870
I changed schools again and again.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:49.870
And it never took long for people
to find out I had no parents.

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:53.870
But I didn't give in. Do you know why?

00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:01.000
I saw my brother every Sunday,
and he'd make me a simple meal.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.330
That made me so happy.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.500
Someday, we would open a restaurant.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.870
One where, no matter how sad
a person was when they arrived,

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:10.700
they'd be sure to leave
with a smile on their face.

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:14.040
Because that was our dream!

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:17.700
And you took that from us!

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:20.750
Eiji, because you stomped on his knee,

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:24.450
Tsukasa-san was forced to leave
the restaurant where he worked.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:28.410
I didn't know.

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:32.120
It was the first time I'd ever
been violent toward someone.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:35.580
I'm sorry! Someday I'll get a real job,
and I'll make up for it!

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.580
Liar!

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:40.790
I know how you live your life!

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:44.290
All you do is wander around every day!

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.620
That's not true.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:48.580
It's not like that.

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:51.790
Ever since I got out of juvie,
it's like there are high walls everywhere.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.410
"Daily Job Offers"

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.410
Ever since I got out of juvie,
it's like there are high walls everywhere.

00:17:53.410 --> 00:17:55.620
Ever since I got out of juvie,
it's like there are high walls everywhere.

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:58.040
I can't make it over them!

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:04.200
No one's going to sympathize with you.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:06.580
Your wrongdoing won't disappear.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:10.580
And Tsukasa's leg will
never again be the way it was.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:12.580
Has that hit home yet?

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.330
Yes, sir.

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:20.830
Now that you've accepted all that,
think about what you can do from now on.

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:22.950
Take your time.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:26.660
We'll wait for your answer,
however long we must.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:08.250
I'm no stranger to this town. Makoto-kun.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:12.750
I realized you were the famous troubleshooter.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:15.370
Thanks for praising my cooking.

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:21.830
When I spotted you in town,
it made my blood boil.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:27.370
I'm human, too, after all.

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:29.080
But...

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:37.250
You're also human, not a beast.

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.580
I know that now, after listening to you.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.290
Your guilt will probably never go away.

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:51.870
But I'm choosing to forgive you.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.700
Tsukasa! Are you sure?!

00:19:55.700 --> 00:20:01.540
I'm sure. If I worry over it forever,
my tomorrow will never begin.

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:41.950
I get it.

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:45.290
What you did was "restorative justice."

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:46.250
Huh?

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:49.750
It's a method that's slowly
being adopted in Japan.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:53.330
The victim and perpetrator meet
and speak face to face

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:56.910
in order to aid the victim's recovery
and the perp's rehabilitation.

00:20:56.910 --> 00:21:00.000
In other words, an attempt at a reunion.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.580
Reunion?

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:04.700
One of restoration, of rebuilding.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.830
Makes sense.

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.950
You've done well, Makoto.

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:12.620
It's strange for me to say this,
as the Ikebukuro Chief of Police,

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:17.250
but I get the feeling this town
will be safe as long as you're around.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.160
Don't know what you're talking about.

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:28.580
Later on, Takashi and Eiji
met with the four extorters.

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:31.830
He made them promise to return
all the money they'd ever extorted

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:36.250
and never to approach Eiji again.

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:39.200
It was discipline done right.

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:47.450
The Hayama siblings told me
they plan to start a food truck someday.

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:51.330
Believe it or not, Eiji's going to help out, too.

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:57.080
In the end, we were all residents
of this peaceful town of Ikebukuro.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:00.000
Meaning, we were people
who could cast aside hatred

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.370
in order to get started on tomorrow.
